      "math_academy_id": "q-225058",
      "sequence_position": 3,
      "problem": "Using the cumulative distribution function table of the Poisson random variable $X∼\\text{Po}(9)$ given below, compute $P(4\\le X\\le 7).$\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ | $6$ | $7$ | $8$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $P(X\\le x)$ | $\\,0.0062\\,$ | $\\,0.0212\\,$ | $\\,0.0550\\,$ | $\\,0.1157\\,$ | $\\,0.2068\\,$ | $\\,0.3239\\,$ | $\\,0.4557\\,$ |\n\n$P(4\\le X\\le 7)=$\n{{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $X$ is a function $F(x)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x).\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(7) & =P(X\\le 7) \\\\  & =P(X\\in \\{0,1,…,7\\}) \\\\  & =P(X\\in \\{0,1,2,3\\})+P(X\\in \\{4,5,6,7\\}) \\\\  & =P(X\\le 3)+P(4\\le X\\le 7) \\\\  & =F(3)+P(4\\le X\\le 7).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(4\\le X\\le 7) & =F(7)-F(3) \\\\  & =0.3239-0.0212 \\\\  & =0.3027.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
